/* deadmsg.rcss - DeathMsgPanel layout, from the old
   abcenchance/res/DeathMsgPanel.res (rs1.1 anchor = right inset 20dp,
   ypos 30, 200 wide, 60 tall). Newest row at the bottom (old
   reverse-iterate PerformLayout bottom-anchored the rows inside the
   60dp-tall box); each row: attacker | [inflictor] | victim, right-packed.
   Colours are the old scheme DeathMsgPanel.* values.

   Motion (the chat log's arrival, chat.rcss): a new row rises 7dp from
   under its slot while it fades in, and the feed glides its viewport to
   the tail instead of letting the reflow jump the rows one height up -
   see followTail in KillFeedModule.cpp.

   The feed is therefore two shells. #feed is the scroll viewport: it
   stays 60dp tall and scrolls programmatically only (RmlUi computes the
   scrollable overflow for `hidden` but builds no scrollbar widgets, and
   the panel document is pointer-transparent, so nothing can scroll it by
   hand). #stack is the bottom-packed row stack: `min-height` keeps the
   rows hugging the viewport's bottom while the rows are shallower than
   the box, and past capacity the stack grows out of the viewport's
   bottom-right scrollable overflow instead of spilling out of its top,
   which is what gives the glide a range to cover. */

#deadmsg {
	position: absolute;
	right: 20dp;
	top: 30dp;
	width: 200dp;
	height: 60dp;
	overflow: hidden;
}

#deadmsg #feed {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0dp;
	top: 0dp;
	width: 200dp;
	height: 100%;
	overflow: hidden;
}

#deadmsg #stack {
	display: flex;
	flex-flow: column;
	justify-content: flex-end;
	min-height: 100%;
}

/* New-row entrance: a row rises from just under its slot while it fades
   in, so a burst reads as kills stacking up from the feed's bottom edge
   instead of blinking on. RmlUi (re)starts an animation whenever the
   computed `animation` value changes, and the panel never touches that
   property after a row is appended, so every row plays this exactly
   once. */
@keyframes deadmsg-row-enter {
	from {
		transform: translateY(7dp);
		opacity: 0;
	}
	to {
		transform: translateY(0dp);
		opacity: 1;
	}
}

#deadmsg .row {
	position: relative;
	flex: none;
	/* Old CDeathMsgItem::PerformLayout sized the row's background to the
	   three labels' content width and right-packed it inside the 200dp
	   panel - a short kill feed row must not paint a full-width box. */
	align-self: flex-end;
	width: auto;
	display: flex;
	flex-flow: row;
	justify-content: flex-end;
	background-color: #7d7d7d7d;
	border-radius: 4dp;
	padding: 1dp 2dp;
	margin-bottom: 1dp;
	animation: deadmsg-row-enter 0.18s cubic-out;
}

#deadmsg .attacker {
	color: #ff0000;
}
#deadmsg .inflictor {
	color: #ffffff;
	margin: 0dp 1dp;
}
#deadmsg .victim {
	color: #64c882;
}
